; Install the FujiNet NIO driver and tools on Workbench 2.04 (Kickstart 2.0x).
;
; Run it from the NIO disk:
;   Execute NIO:Install-FujiNet-WB204
;
; It installs the Kickstart 1.3 (nix13) builds, which use only V33 calls and
; run unchanged on 2.04. The drivers are loaded at boot from S:User-Startup,
; which the 2.04 Startup-Sequence runs when it exists.
; Disk image mounting (FMOUNT, FUMOUNT, FBOOT) is not set up by this script.
; It is safe to run again.

FailAt 21

Copy NIO:fujinet-nio.device TO DEVS: QUIET
Copy NIO:fujinet-disk.device TO DEVS: QUIET
Copy NIO:fujinet-load-resident TO C: QUIET
Copy NIO:fujinet-mount TO C: QUIET
Copy NIO:fujinet-nio-exchange TO C: QUIET
Copy NIO:fapp TO C: QUIET
Copy NIO:fdrive TO C: QUIET
Copy NIO:fhost TO C: QUIET
Copy NIO:fin TO C: QUIET
Copy NIO:fls TO C: QUIET
Copy NIO:fout TO C: QUIET

If NOT EXISTS S:User-Startup
  Echo >S:User-Startup "; User-Startup"
EndIf

Search >NIL: S:User-Startup "fujinet-load-resident" QUIET
If WARN
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "C:fujinet-load-resident DEVS:fujinet-nio.device fujinet-nio.device"
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "C:fujinet-load-resident DEVS:fujinet-disk.device fujinet-disk.device"
  Echo "Added the FujiNet drivers to S:User-Startup."
Else
  Echo "S:User-Startup already loads the FujiNet drivers; left it unchanged."
EndIf

Echo "FujiNet installed. Reboot to load the drivers."
Echo "Until then, Execute NIO:Run-xkcd loads the driver and starts xkcd."
